      "created_at": "2024-09-11T01:18:47.448Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote quote-modified\" data-post=\"4\" data-topic=\"42604\">\n  <div class=\"title\">\n    <div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n    <img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/user_avatar/discuss.frappe.io/revant_one/48/55081_2.png\" class=\"avatar\">\n    <a href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/t/frappe-oauth-how-to-disable-native-login-form/42604/4\">Frappe OAuth - How to disable native login form</a> <a class=\"badge-category__wrapper \" href=\"/c/framework/customization/28\"><span data-category-id=\"28\" style=\"--category-badge-color: #3AB54A; --category-badge-text-color: #FFFFFF; --parent-category-badge-color: #F7941D;\" data-parent-category-id=\"5\" data-drop-close=\"true\" class=\"badge-category --has-parent\"><span class=\"badge-category__name\">Customization</span></span></a>\n  </div>\n  <blockquote>\n    Workaround (no custom app) \nAdd following script to Website Script or custom Website Theme: \n// Detect login page\nif ($('#page-login').length) {\n    // Hide page\n    $('body').hide();\n\n    // Login using custom social login button\n    const loginBtn = $('.btn-castlecraft').length\n        ? $('.btn-castlecraft')[0]\n        : undefined;\n    loginBtn &amp;&amp; loginBtn.click();\n}\n\nNote : replace .btn-castlecraft with your button’s class name in above code. \nAdditionally, do the following if required: \n\ndi…\n  </blockquote>\n</aside>\n",
